.TH "SKARN-SERVE" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.17.0" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-serve \- Start the local web UI (search, recent, stats, and a redacted
scan view) bound to 127.0.0.1
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBserve\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start the local web UI (search, recent, stats, and a redacted scan view) bound
to 127.0.0.1.
.PP
Control the localhost web UI. Access requires the per\-run token embedded in
the URL the command prints at startup; opening that URL sets a session cookie,
and scripts may pass it as a token= query parameter instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fIn\fR
Port to listen on; 0 asks the OS to assign one. Always binds 127.0.0.1 only.
The default is 7777.
.TP
\fB\-\-rules\fR \fIpath\fR
Load a custom TOML rules file in addition to the bundled rules; the web
Security scan then also surfaces its findings.
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\fR \fIpath\fR
Suppress findings recorded in this accepted\-findings baseline; the Security
view hides them by default behind a show/hide toggle. Without this flag,
~/.config/skarn/baseline.json is applied automatically when it exists. A
directory of baselines (the org form) requires a Team license.
